-- ── Welcome card ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

UPDATE components SET data = '{
  "html": "<h2>What you are looking at</h2><p>This is a fully working full-stack web application — not a tutorial, not a scaffold with placeholder pages, but a real system with user authentication, a database, file storage, dynamic forms, a content management system, and an AI integration. Everything you see here is live and editable. The App Guide documents every feature. The Developer Guide explains how the code works and how to extend it.</p><p>ManuSpine started as the internal infrastructure of <strong>ManuLab</strong> — a personal platform for financial tracking, clinical research, and data analysis built by a biomedical engineer. After building enough features on the same foundation, the scaffolding became worth sharing. ManuSpine is that foundation, cleaned up and open-sourced so anyone can clone it and build their own product on top.</p><h3>What you can use it for</h3><p><strong>Learning.</strong> If you want to understand how a real full-stack application is structured, this is a concrete working example. JWT authentication, role-based access, GraphQL and REST APIs, database-driven dynamic forms, Docker multi-service orchestration, object storage, real-time streaming, AI integration — all of it is here, wired together and running, not explained in isolation.</p><p><strong>Building.</strong> Add your own domain (your feature, your data model, your idea) and you start with auth, forms, file storage, and a content system already working. The five-layer domain pattern — SQL table, Express route, GraphQL resolver, optional Python computation, React page — is consistent across every feature. Learn it once and you can add anything.</p><h3>Built with Claude Code</h3><p>ManuSpine was developed with <strong>Claude Code</strong> as a development partner throughout the entire project. Claude Code is an AI coding assistant that reads the project conventions from <code>CLAUDE.md</code> and works alongside you in the terminal or your IDE. It helped write routes, scaffold domains, debug queries, and document the codebase you are reading right now.</p><p>If you are new to full-stack development, this is encouraging: you do not have to figure everything out alone. The same AI that helped build this project is available to help you extend it. Describe a feature in plain language and Claude Code will scaffold the SQL, the API, and the React page in one pass. See <strong>Developer Guide → Claude Code</strong> to get started.</p><h3>The stack</h3><ul><li><strong>React + Ionic</strong> — frontend, cross-platform (web now, mobile with Capacitor when needed)</li><li><strong>Express + GraphQL</strong> — Node.js backend; minimal and explicit, no framework magic</li><li><strong>FastAPI</strong> — Python computation layer, stateless by design</li><li><strong>PostgreSQL</strong> — database with JSONB for flexible node data</li><li><strong>MinIO</strong> — S3-compatible file storage, runs in Docker alongside everything else</li></ul><p>Everything runs with one command from the repo root: <code>./run</code>.</p>"
}' WHERE name = 'welcome_card';


